CPU and memory stress, two partitions
=====================================

A stress test that uses the CPU and memory at a balanced rate, in two identical
partitions, to study interference between partitions.

What it tests
-------------

Execution time of matrix generation and multiplication when two partitions with
the same workload share the processor and memory.

What it does
------------

Two partitions, P1 and P2, each with six periodic processes.

Each partition has a generator process that fills two 500x500 matrices and five
processes that multiply them, each taking a fifth of the rows (NB_DIVISIONS =
5). Period 10 s; each partition has a 2 s window in a 4 s major frame.

Expected output
---------------

"[Part n] Generating matrix A and B", "Done multiplying rows a to rows b" from
both partitions.

Build and run
-------------

From the top-level directory (builds every benchmark; QEMU needs only the one):

    make benchmarks                     # x86_64
    make BSP=arm64-qemu benchmarks      # arm64

    qemu-system-x86_64 -vga none -m 1G -nographic \
        -kernel benchmark/CPU_MEM_2PART/build/x86_64-qemu/pok.elf
    qemu-system-aarch64 -M virt -cpu cortex-a53 -m 1G -nographic \
        -kernel benchmark/CPU_MEM_2PART/build/arm64-qemu/pok.elf

To build only this benchmark, run "scons bsp=x86_64-qemu" (or bsp=arm64-qemu)
in this directory with POK_PATH set. The benchmark runs forever; quit QEMU with
Ctrl-A X.
